      "moduleName": "The Central Idea of VSEPR",
      "description": "Introduces the core principle of VSEPR theory: electron domains around a central atom repel each other and arrange to maximize their separation. Students see a central atom accumulate electron domains that push apart into a minimum-repulsion configuration.",
      "author": "A Robot",
      "institution": "MTSU",
      "dateCreated": "2026-07-10",
      "educationalObjectives": [
        "State the central premise of VSEPR: electron domains arrange to minimize mutual repulsion.",
        "Determine the steric number of a central atom by counting bonding pairs and lone pairs.",
        "Relate the number of electron domains to their spatial arrangement."
      ],
      "instructions": [
        "Watch how electron domains push apart around the central atom.",
        "Use Next and Previous to move through the demonstration.",
        "Count the domains at each step to track the steric number."
